Ladybird’s Event Timing still creates an entry for every event it
times, and builds the target’s selector when the event’s processing
ends, as the spec says. Blink does both too: WindowPerformance creates a
PerformanceEventTiming for each timed event, and WindowPerformance::
EventTimingProcessingEnd() sets the entry’s target selector. The changes
here are in how Ladybird does that work, which has no counterpart to
compare. That’s from reading the source.
